double A = 5.678;
out.printf("%.1f\n",A);
out.print("Five\nSix");
out.println("Seven\nEight");

questions.explanation:
out.printf("%.1f\n",A);
This prints A formatted with one decimal place (rounded) followed by a carriage return
out.print("Five\nSix");
On the next line, this prints "Five" on the next line, then "Six" on the following line because of
the "\n"
out.println("Seven\nEight");
This prints "Seven" next to "Six." The \n sends "Eight " to the last line.

